     "good": "All headers, names, symbols, and commands stay on one line. The identifying columns are easy to scan.",
     "problems": "The meanings form narrow blocks, making the rows tall and leaving substantial empty space beside the shorter identifiers.",
     "cause": "The 137px Name column reserves enough space for Tensor product on one line, leaving only 277px for Meaning."
    },
    {
     "design": "r0B",
     "good": "The wider Meaning column improves prose flow and reduces row heights. Tensor product wraps cleanly, while headers, individual words, symbols, and commands remain intact. Rows still read clearly across the table.",
     "problems": "The Integral explanation ends with a short final line, and the wrapped name takes two lines.",
     "cause": "Meaning has 306px, which is insufficient to avoid every short line. Name has 108px, so Tensor product wraps at its word boundary."
    },
    {
     "design": "r0C",
     "good": "Headers, symbols, commands, and individual words remain intact, and the identifying columns are spacious.",
     "problems": "The meanings are compressed into tall, narrow blocks, creating the longest rows and large areas of empty space in the identifying columns. Tensor product still wraps.",
     "cause": "The 105px Symbol and LaTeX columns and 126px Name column leave only 247px for Meaning; the extra Name width is still insufficient to keep Tensor product on one line."
    }
   ],
